{"blob":"5510dcc24130bb5dcb92ce61b2764b11055968a9","blocks":[{"anchor":"\"\"\"","lines":"1-216","text":"The module documents the device-link responsibilities, event-log invariants, and logging constraints. Constants and a small bundled-schema interpreter define message limits, stream types, and validation rules.","title":"Protocol contract and schema interpreter"},{"anchor":"class _Invalid(Exception):","lines":"217-451","text":"Schema helpers validate or clean JSON values, then the dataclasses describe accepted events, errors, run state, welcome metadata, statistics, and callbacks.","title":"Validation and public value types"},{"anchor":"class _Run:","lines":"454-656","text":"Internal run and pending-request records support correlation. Frame helpers build and parse protocol envelopes, judge welcomes, sanitize error details, and recover a contiguous server cursor from SQLite.","title":"Run cursors and frame helpers"},{"anchor":"class DeviceLink:","lines":"662-900","text":"DeviceLink initializes injected transport and timing dependencies, exposes state counters, starts supervision, waits for state changes, and finalizes pending requests during shutdown.","title":"Link state and lifecycle"},{"anchor":"    async def run(self) -> None:","lines":"903-1047","text":"The supervision loop retries classified failures with backoff. Each attempt loads and checks credentials, performs the handshake, resumes active runs, starts keepalive, and cleans up the socket.","title":"Connect, authenticate, reconnect"},{"anchor":"    async def _read(self, ws: Any) -> BaseException:","lines":"1050-1204","text":"Incoming frames are parsed without leaking content through tracebacks, dispatched to pong, error, or stream handlers, and accepted stream events are checked for duplicates and sequence gaps before storage.","title":"Receive and persist server messages"},{"anchor":"    def _resume_payload(self, run: _Run, state: Mapping[str, Any] | None = None) -> dict[str, Any]:","lines":"1207-1315","